WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.356
Hi, I'm Bitsy!

00:00:02.356 --> 00:00:05.200
Audio8 open-sourced eight audio checkpoints in two months.

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:09.466
Here's how its speech recognizer hears, and what each size ships with.

00:00:10.933 --> 00:00:16.336
Each recognizer is a Whisper-style audio encoder bolted onto a small language model.

00:00:16.336 --> 00:00:20.076
Merged audio frames drop in where placeholder tokens sit.

00:00:21.508 --> 00:00:25.600
Sound becomes a log-mel spectrogram, and a Whisper-style encoder turns it into

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:26.964
a stream of frames.

00:00:27.384 --> 00:00:32.294
An MLP adapter merges consecutive frames, four at a time in the smallest model.

00:00:32.714 --> 00:00:37.441
Those embeddings replace dedicated audio placeholder tokens in the text sequence.

00:00:37.861 --> 00:00:41.470
A Qwen-style causal decoder reads it all and writes the transcript.

00:00:42.733 --> 00:00:44.655
One model only transcribes speech.

00:00:46.407 --> 00:00:47.960
The other also speaks.

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:53.006
Yet its encoder, adapter and decoder layers match the first, parameter for parameter.

00:00:54.175 --> 00:00:58.248
That encoder is a fixed six hundred and thirty-seven million parameters, so

00:00:58.248 --> 00:01:02.321
every size name undercounts: the smallest by three point one three times,

00:01:02.321 --> 00:01:04.697
the largest by one point three five.

00:01:06.258 --> 00:01:08.941
Quantization pays close to its nominal rate.

00:01:08.941 --> 00:01:13.539
In the smallest model's ONNX bundle, four-bit shrinks the decoder cache seven

00:01:13.539 --> 00:01:15.072
point four five times.

00:01:16.775 --> 00:01:20.845
The smallest recognizer gets the full ladder: three ONNX precisions, and a

00:01:20.845 --> 00:01:22.880
Core ML build for the iPhone.

00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:25.361
The middle tier gets one precision each.

00:01:26.009 --> 00:01:31.529
And the most downloaded model, the 3B recognizer, has no official export at all.

00:01:31.529 --> 00:01:33.501
Community conversions fill the gap.

00:01:35.183 --> 00:01:38.078
One architecture serves every size, and even synthesis.

00:01:38.078 --> 00:01:42.420
The deployment work is richest where it is easiest: the small end.

00:01:43.858 --> 00:01:47.755
To recap: an encoder, an adapter and a decoder, shared across jobs,

00:01:47.755 --> 00:01:50.679
with builds that thin out as the models grow.

00:01:51.099 --> 00:01:53.191
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:53.191 --> 00:01:53.788
I'm Bitsy.

00:01:53.788 --> 00:01:54.087
Bye!
